@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] personal-android-storage-is-keystore-backed
Android personal sessions MUST use a separate non-exportable Android Keystore AES-GCM
key and an authenticated versioned, bounded, atomically replaced blob in no-backup
storage. Neither pending nor accepted personal sessions MAY fall back to ordinary
preferences, legacy account storage or plaintext files. Read/write failures MUST retain
fixed safe errors. A successful write MUST sync and verify its committed ciphertext
before secure staging permits server confirmation. A failed post-commit verification
MUST NOT roll back the already committed file. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 any-account GitHub request and the accepted
22 Oct separate native secure-staging boundary.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] personal-origin-is-app-configured
Personal sign-in MUST use the app-owned HTTPS origin selected at build configuration,
independent of legacy Settings/Access. An unconfigured build MUST keep public browsing
available and MUST NOT invent a successful connection or probe a legacy server. A
verified public-only profile MUST remain in the personal/Explore flow. A freshly verified
privateRepositories session MUST directly mount the complete production native Home,
Profile, Settings and review services through its own captured workspace capability,
without any legacy credentials/preferences or second Pully/Access sign-in. Its bearer
MUST NOT go to GitHub REST. This intentionally replaces the limited personal Home by
Tavi25Oct2026, one GitHub login and the full production UI. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 public
browsing/personal-account decision and approved 22 Oct native connection implementation.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] saved-personal-settings-are-local-preferences-only
Cold local preference selection MAY read only a securely accepted private account's
opaque namespace for the configured personal origin. A pending/public-only record,
different origin, failed secure-store probe or successful local sign-out MUST yield
no private preference owner. This lookup MUST NOT restore a visible account, create a
workspace, send a bearer or authorize any request. Source: Tavi's 25 Oct 2026 #1/#7
cold update-notification integration requirement.
The local-only background preference reader MUST use an independent vault snapshot,
rather than the UI-confined mutable runtime vault. Native secure blob reads and writes
MUST serialize across storage instances so AtomicFile recovery cannot race a writer.
